/--------------------------------------------------------------------
/ TELEMAC3D steering generated by hydromate for case 'ering'
/ v9+ checked variant: true 2D continuation from r2d.slf
/ non-hydrostatic; sigma layers
/--------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE : 'ering 3D non-hydrostatic - 2D continuation'
/
/ INPUT / OUTPUT FILES
GEOMETRY FILE : geometry.slf
BOUNDARY CONDITIONS FILE : boundaries.cli
3D RESULT FILE : r3d.slf
2D RESULT FILE : r3d-2d.slf
MASS-BALANCE : YES
/
/ HOTSTART FROM THE 2D STEADY RUN
/ TELEMAC v9+: FILE FOR 2D CONTINUATION is sufficient; old 2D CONTINUATION keyword is removed.
/ Use r2d_hotstart.slf instead if that is the exact 2D state you want to lift to 3D.
FILE FOR 2D CONTINUATION : r2d.slf
FILE FOR 2D CONTINUATION FORMAT : 'SERAFIN'
INITIAL TIME SET TO ZERO : YES
/ Fallback only if 2D continuation fails on dry banks:
/ INITIAL CONDITIONS : 'CONSTANT DEPTH'
/ INITIAL DEPTH : 0.921
VARIABLES FOR 2D GRAPHIC PRINTOUTS : 'U,V,H,S,B,F'
VARIABLES FOR 3D GRAPHIC PRINTOUTS : 'Z,U,V,W,NUX,NUZ'
/
/ VERTICAL MESH
NUMBER OF HORIZONTAL LEVELS : 5
MESH TRANSFORMATION : 1
/
/ TIME
TIME STEP : 0.14
NUMBER OF TIME STEPS : 4489
GRAPHIC PRINTOUT PERIOD : 224
LISTING PRINTOUT PERIOD : 112
/
/ STOP CRITERIA
STOP IF A STEADY STATE IS REACHED : YES
STOP CRITERIA : 1.E-3;1.E-3;1.E-3
/
/ NON-HYDROSTATIC SOLVER
NON-HYDROSTATIC VERSION : YES
SOLVER FOR PPE : 7
/ Default since v8.1 is 1.E-4; 1.E-6 is usually unnecessarily strict for spin-up.
ACCURACY FOR PPE : 1.E-4
/
/ NUMERICS
/ With tidal flats, TELEMAC-3D docs recommend PSI/LIPS/NERD-compatible advection treatment.
SCHEME FOR ADVECTION OF VELOCITIES : 5
SCHEME OPTION FOR ADVECTION OF VELOCITIES : 4
SCHEME FOR ADVECTION OF K-EPSILON : 5
SCHEME OPTION FOR ADVECTION OF K-EPSILON : 4
SOLVER FOR PROPAGATION : 2
ACCURACY FOR PROPAGATION : 1.E-6
MAXIMUM NUMBER OF ITERATIONS FOR PROPAGATION : 200
MATRIX STORAGE : 3
FREE SURFACE GRADIENT COMPATIBILITY : 0.1
IMPLICITATION FOR DEPTH : 0.55
IMPLICITATION FOR VELOCITIES : 0.55
INITIAL GUESS FOR DEPTH : 1
TIDAL FLATS : YES
MASS-LUMPING FOR DEPTH : 1.
MASS-LUMPING FOR VELOCITIES : 1.
TREATMENT OF NEGATIVE DEPTHS : 2
MINIMAL VALUE FOR DEPTH : 0.0115
/
/ TURBULENCE: kept as k-epsilon, matching the 2D turbulence-model class.
HORIZONTAL TURBULENCE MODEL : 3
VERTICAL TURBULENCE MODEL : 3
/
/ FRICTION: bottom Nikuradse law retained, but note that the 2D zonal friction.tbl is not represented here.
LAW OF BOTTOM FRICTION : 5
FRICTION COEFFICIENT FOR THE BOTTOM : 0.2
/
/ BOUNDARY CONDITIONS
PRESCRIBED FLOWRATES : 0.;2.0000
PRESCRIBED ELEVATIONS : 329.2650;0.
/ Horizontal profiles kept consistent with the 2D setup.
VELOCITY PROFILES : 1;4
VELOCITY VERTICAL PROFILES : 2;2
&ETA
